IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc24-appeal-scc.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part XXI, sections 691 to 696:
-- Appeals to the Supreme Court of Canada, and Appeals by the Attorney General of Canada.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), part agent ccc24. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How to read an answer: see the header of ccc24-appeal-procedure.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING; a caller must never turn NOTHING into JUST FALSE).

§ `Part XXI -- Appeals to the Supreme Court of Canada (sections 691 to 696)`

§§ `Section 691 -- Appeal from conviction; appeal where acquittal set aside`

-- 691(1): the two grounds are "(a) any question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents" and "(b) any question of law, if leave to appeal is granted".
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14337 | 691 (1) A person who is convicted of an indictable offence and whose conviction is affirmed by the court of appeal may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada
-- src:14338 | (a) on any question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents; or
-- src:14339 | (b) on any question of law, if leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada.
@ref s 691(1) (src:14337-14339)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conviction is affirmed by the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is on a question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is on a question of law and leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 691(1) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the conviction` MEANS
    IF    `the person is convicted of an indictable offence`
      AND `the conviction is affirmed by the court of appeal`
      AND (`the appeal is on a question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents` OR `the appeal is on a question of law and leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on any question of law, if leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada"

-- 691(2): acquittal "other than by reason of a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder", set aside by the court of appeal.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14341 | (2) A person who is acquitted of an indictable offence other than by reason of a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder and whose acquittal is set aside by the court of appeal may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada
-- src:14342 | (a) on any question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents;
-- src:14343 | (b) on any question of law, if the Court of Appeal enters a verdict of guilty against the person; or
-- src:14344 | (c) on any question of law, if leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada.
@ref s 691(2) (src:14341-14344)
GIVEN `the person is acquitted of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acquittal is by reason of a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acquittal is set aside by the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is on a question of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a judge of the court of appeal dissents on the question of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court of Appeal enters a verdict of guilty against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal` MEANS
    IF    `the person is acquitted of an indictable offence`
      AND (NOT `the acquittal is by reason of a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`)
      AND `the acquittal is set aside by the court of appeal`
      AND `the appeal is on a question of law`
      AND (`a judge of the court of appeal dissents on the question of law` OR `the Court of Appeal enters a verdict of guilty against the person` OR `leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than by reason of a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder and whose acquittal is set aside by the court of appeal"

§§ `Section 692 -- Appeal against affirmation of a verdict of not criminally responsible or unfit to stand trial`

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14346 | 692 (1) A person who has been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder and
-- src:14347 | (a) whose verdict is affirmed on that ground by the court of appeal, or
-- src:14348 | (b) against whom a verdict of guilty is entered by the court of appeal under subparagraph 686(4)(b)(ii),
-- src:14349 | may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada.
@ref s 692(1) (src:14346-14349)
GIVEN `the person has been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the verdict is affirmed on that ground by the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a verdict of guilty is entered against the person by the court of appeal under subparagraph 686(4)(b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 692(1) the person found not criminally responsible may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` MEANS
    IF `the person has been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` AND (`the verdict is affirmed on that ground by the court of appeal` OR `a verdict of guilty is entered against the person by the court of appeal under subparagraph 686(4)(b)(ii)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whose verdict is affirmed on that ground by the court of appeal"

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14351 | (2) A person who is found unfit to stand trial and against whom that verdict is affirmed by the court of appeal may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada.
@ref s 692(2) (src:14351-14351)
GIVEN `the person is found unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the verdict is affirmed by the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 692(2) the person found unfit to stand trial may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` MEANS
    IF `the person is found unfit to stand trial` AND `the verdict is affirmed by the court of appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is found unfit to stand trial and against whom that verdict is affirmed by the court of appeal may appeal"

-- src:14353 | (3) An appeal under subsection (1) or (2) may be
-- src:14354 | (a) on any question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents; or
-- src:14355 | (b) on any question of law, if leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada.
@ref s 692(3) (src:14353-14355)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is on a question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is on a question of law and leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 692(3) an appeal under subsection (1) or (2) may be on the ground` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is an appeal under subsection (1) or (2)` AND (`the appeal is on a question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents` OR `the appeal is on a question of law and leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) on any question of law, if leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada"

§§ `Section 693 -- Appeal by Attorney General`

-- 693(1) and (2): "Where" is a where-gate on a grant: JUST FALSE by ruling (b), listed for a lawyer.
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14357 | 693 (1) Where a judgment of a court of appeal sets aside a conviction pursuant to an appeal taken under section 675 or dismisses an appeal taken pursuant to paragraph 676(1)(a), (b) or (c) or subsection 676(3), the Attorney General may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada
-- src:14358 | (a) on any question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents; or
-- src:14359 | (b) on any question of law, if leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada.
@ref s 693(1) (src:14357-14359)
GIVEN `a judgment of a court of appeal sets aside a conviction pursuant to an appeal taken under section 675 or dismisses an appeal taken pursuant to paragraph 676(1)(a), (b) or (c) or subsection 676(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant is the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is on a question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is on a question of law and leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693(1) the Attorney General may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a judgment of a court of appeal sets aside a conviction pursuant to an appeal taken under section 675 or dismisses an appeal taken pursuant to paragraph 676(1)(a), (b) or (c) or subsection 676(3)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a judgment of a court of appeal sets aside a conviction pursuant to an appeal taken under section 675"
        IF `the appellant is the Attorney General` AND (`the appeal is on a question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents` OR `the appeal is on a question of law and leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on any question of law, if leave to appeal is granted by the Supreme Court of Canada"

-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14361 | (2) Where leave to appeal is granted under paragraph (1)(b), the Supreme Court of Canada may impose such terms as it sees fit.
@ref s 693(2) (src:14361-14361)
GIVEN `leave to appeal is granted under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693(2) the Supreme Court of Canada may impose such terms as it sees fit on the grant of leave to appeal` MEANS
    IF `leave to appeal is granted under paragraph (1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where leave to appeal is granted under paragraph (1)(b)"

§§ `Section 694 -- Notice of appeal`

-- 694: "No appeal lies to the Supreme Court of Canada unless notice of appeal in writing is served". The function answers the one limb the text states: whether that notice requirement is met.
-- The Supreme Court Act's own rules of service are outside the text: an input.
-- src:14363 | 694 No appeal lies to the Supreme Court of Canada unless notice of appeal in writing is served by the appellant on the respondent in accordance with the Supreme Court Act.
@ref s 694 (src:14363-14363)
GIVEN `notice of appeal in writing has been served by the appellant on the respondent in accordance with the Supreme Court Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694 notice of appeal in writing has been served by the appellant on the respondent in accordance with the Supreme Court Act` MEANS
    IF `notice of appeal in writing has been served by the appellant on the respondent in accordance with the Supreme Court Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless notice of appeal in writing is served by the appellant on the respondent in accordance with the Supreme Court Act"

§§ `Section 694.1 -- Legal assistance for accused`

-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14365 | 694.1 (1) The Supreme Court of Canada or a judge thereof may, at any time, assign counsel to act on behalf of an accused who is a party to an appeal to the Court or to proceedings preliminary or incidental to an appeal to the Court where, in the opinion of the Court or judge, it appears desirable in the interests of justice that the accused should have legal assistance and where it appears that the accused has not sufficient means to obtain that assistance.
@ref s 694.1(1) (src:14365-14365)
GIVEN `the accused is a party to an appeal to the Court or to proceedings preliminary or incidental to an appeal to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Court or judge it appears desirable in the interests of justice that the accused should have legal assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears that the accused has not sufficient means to obtain that assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694.1(1) the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge may assign counsel to act on behalf of an accused who is a party to an appeal to the Court` MEANS
    IF `the accused is a party to an appeal to the Court or to proceedings preliminary or incidental to an appeal to the Court` AND `in the opinion of the Court or judge it appears desirable in the interests of justice that the accused should have legal assistance` AND `it appears that the accused has not sufficient means to obtain that assistance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where, in the opinion of the Court or judge, it appears desirable in the interests of justice that the accused should have legal assistance and where it appears that the accused has not sufficient means to obtain that assistance"

-- src:14367 | (2) Where counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection (1) and legal aid is not granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program, the fees and disbursements of counsel shall be paid by the Attorney General who is the appellant or respondent, as the case may be, in the appeal.
@ref s 694.1(2) (src:14367-14367)
GIVEN `counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `legal aid is not granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694.1(2) the fees and disbursements of the assigned counsel shall be paid by the Attorney General who is the appellant or respondent` MEANS
    IF `counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection (1)` AND `legal aid is not granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where counsel is assigned pursuant to subsection (1) and legal aid is not granted to the accused pursuant to a provincial legal aid program"

-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14369 | (3) Where subsection (2) applies and counsel and the Attorney General cannot agree on fees or disbursements of counsel, the Attorney General or the counsel may apply to the Registrar of the Supreme Court of Canada, and the Registrar may tax the disputed fees and disbursements.
@ref s 694.1(3) (src:14369-14369)
GIVEN `subsection (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `counsel and the Attorney General cannot agree on fees or disbursements of counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694.1(3) the Attorney General or the counsel may apply to the Registrar of the Supreme Court of Canada to tax the disputed fees and disbursements` MEANS
    IF `subsection (2) applies` AND `counsel and the Attorney General cannot agree on fees or disbursements of counsel`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where subsection (2) applies and counsel and the Attorney General cannot agree on fees or disbursements of counsel"

§§ `Section 694.2 -- Right of appellant to attend`

DECLARE `s 694.2(2) proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `s 694.2(2)(a) an application for leave to appeal`
    `s 694.2(2)(b) a proceeding that is preliminary or incidental to an appeal`
    `s 694.2(2)(c) the hearing of the appeal`
    `s 694.2(2) another proceeding`

-- JUST TRUE here means the bar applies; "unless rules of court provide that entitlement or the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge thereof gives the appellant leave" closes it.
-- @tag fork=F688
-- src:14373 | (2) An appellant who is in custody and who is represented by counsel is not entitled to be present before the Supreme Court of Canada
-- src:14374 | (a) on an application for leave to appeal,
-- src:14375 | (b) on any proceedings that are preliminary or incidental to an appeal, or
-- src:14376 | (c) at the hearing of the appeal,
-- src:14377 | unless rules of court provide that entitlement or the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge thereof gives the appellant leave to be present.
@ref s 694.2(2) (src:14373-14377)
GIVEN `the appellant is in custody and is represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      proceeding IS A `s 694.2(2) proceeding`
      `rules of court provide that the appellant is entitled to be present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge of it gives the appellant leave to be present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694.2(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present before the Supreme Court of Canada applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appellant is in custody and is represented by counsel`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appellant who is in custody and who is represented by counsel"
        IF proceeding EQUALS `s 694.2(2) another proceeding`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "is not entitled to be present before the Supreme Court of Canada"
        IF `rules of court provide that the appellant is entitled to be present` OR `the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge of it gives the appellant leave to be present`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless rules of court provide that entitlement or the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge thereof gives the appellant leave to be present"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 694.2(1): "an appellant who is in custody and who desires to be present ... is entitled": the relative clause identifies the holder, so a person outside it is NOT COVERED.
-- @tag grant=entitled
-- @tag fork=F688
-- src:14371 | 694.2 (1) Subject to subsection (2), an appellant who is in custody and who desires to be present at the hearing of the appeal before the Supreme Court of Canada is entitled to be present at it.
@ref s 694.2(1) (src:14371-14371)
GIVEN `the appellant is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant desires to be present at the hearing of the appeal before the Supreme Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 694.2(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present before the Supreme Court of Canada applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694.2(1) an appellant who is in custody is entitled to be present at the hearing of the appeal before the Supreme Court of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the appellant is in custody` AND `the appellant desires to be present at the hearing of the appeal before the Supreme Court of Canada`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an appellant who is in custody and who desires to be present at the hearing of the appeal"
        IF `s 694.2(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present before the Supreme Court of Canada applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (2)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- the bar of subsection (2) is lifted (JUST FALSE) or not engaged (NOTHING: not represented, or a proceeding it does not name): the entitlement stands

