§§ `Section 696 -- Right of Attorney General of Canada to appeal`

-- src:14387 | 696 The Attorney General of Canada has the same rights of appeal in proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government as the Attorney General of a province has under this Part.
@ref s 696 (src:14387-14387)
GIVEN `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are conducted by or on behalf of the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696 the Attorney General of Canada has the same rights of appeal as the Attorney General of a province has under Part XXI` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada` AND `the proceedings are conducted by or on behalf of the Government of Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government"
